From 6a67ad53f0d1c6638c665dd4538f8e9838c516a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wazer <wazer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:52:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Aquacomputer D5 Next (PID 0xF00E) support

Expose coolant temperature, soft sensors, pump/fan RPM, power and voltage
from the continuous status report (ID 0x01).

Fixed-percent pump and fan duty control via feature report 0x03:
- set channel mode to 0 (direct percent)
- write duty as BE16 centi-percent (same layout as liquidctl)
- CRC-16/USB over the control body
- secondary apply report used by AquaSuite / kernel driver

Control writes are debounced (only on change) and run on a background
thread so FanControl does not freeze on HID feature I/O.

Protocol offsets and control format based on liquidctl and the Linux
aquacomputer_d5next driver. Tested on Windows with FanControl against a
real D5 Next (coolant temp, pump RPM, and pump duty control verified).
